<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kausambi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kaushambi, Kosambi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaushambi was an ancient city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a>, about 50 kilometres south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Prayagraj</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the capital of the Vatsa kingdom. One of the great cities of the Buddha's time, ruled by King Udayana, it lay on trade routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and the west and had important Buddhist monasteries such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghositarama">Ghositarama</a>. Its ruins include massive earthen ramparts and a Mauryan stone pillar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kausambi.jpg" alt="Kausambi" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PHGCOM · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KausambiCastCopperCoin1stCenturyBCEInscribedKosabi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
